Z||000000||Logicdragon||08-09-2001||03:21 PM||||This is my first post, but all in all i've been visiting this site for about 6 months now.  I used to own a 87 fiero gt but I sold it when navy boot camp came calling.  I plan on buying another in a couple of months and i've been looking at different mods already..(I can't wait).  I was wondering,<P>1. I'm thinking about getting an air/fuel ratio gauge and was wondering if anyone could tell me at what ratio(s) the engine should be at.  <P>2.  Also, I don't know if anyone has seen the commercial for bf goodrich tires where the guy pulls up to the beginning of a field and a voice asks him what road he would like, then it validates his tires, then the field turns upside down into a twisty mountain road.  (Great commercial).  At the end of the commercial it says that if you buy some tires now they will give you a digital g-force readout for your car.  Is that a lateral g-force read out or a acceleration g readout?  I would like to buy one but I can't them anywhere on the net.  Anyone know where I might find one?  <P>Thats all.  Thanks.<P>Logicdragon       ||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-09-2001||03:28 PM||||Welcome to the forum! <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com</A>  for the BFG deal. and under full throttle  about 12.5-12.8:1 is nice safe and will have room for improvment. EFI systems makes a fuel injector duty cycle monitor and a/f ratio meter all in the same box get one of those.. i've got one $99 (plus shipping) easy to hook up and WAY more acurate than an autometer unit (had 3 of those) <P><BR>just nticed your in Ca... you might wanna check out <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrantsig.jpg">           <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-09-2001).]||||reg||1
